    <ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>&lt;div&gt;A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;On 1 November 2010, the Minister of Justice introduced Bill C-53, An Act to amend the Criminal Code (mega-trials) (Fair and Efficient Criminal Trials Act), in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bill C-53 amends the Criminal Code. Among other things it&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	allows for the appointment of a judge as a case management judge;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	defines the role and the powers of a case management judge;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	allows a joint hearing of preliminary motions involving similar evidence that arise in related but separate trials.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	allows for delayed severance orders;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	streamlines the use of direct indictments preferred under section 577;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	improves the protection of the identity of jurors;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	increases the maximum number of jurors who can hear the evidence on the merits; and&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	provides that, in the case of a mistrial, certain decisions made during the trial are binding on the parties in any new trial.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>
    <ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>&lt;div&gt;Le Service d'information et de recherche parlementaires de la Bibliothèque du Parlement rédige actuellement le résumé législatif de ce projet de loi et vous propose en attendant le sommaire suivant.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Le 1 novembre 2010, le ministre de la Justice a déposé le projet de loi C-53, Loi modifiant le Code criminel (mégaprocès) (Loi sur la tenue de procès criminels équitables et efficaces),  à la Chambre des communes en première lecture.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Le projet de loi C-53 modifie le Code criminel, et ce, notamment, afin de :&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	permettre la nomination d'un juge à titre de juge responsable de la gestion de l'instance;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	prévoir les attributions du juge responsable de la gestion de l'instance;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	permettre l'audition conjointe des requêtes préliminaires comportant des éléments de preuve similaires qui découlent de procès distincts mais connexes.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	prévoir la prise d'effet ultérieure d'une ordonnance rendue pour la tenue de procès distincts;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	simplifier le recours aux actes d'accusation présentés en vertu de l'article 577;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	renforcer la protection de l'identité des jurés;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	augmenter le nombre maximal de jurés pouvant entendre la preuve sur le fond;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	prévoir qu'en cas d'avortement de procès, certaines décisions rendues dans le cadre de ce procès lient les parties lors de tout nouveau procès.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>
    <ShortLegislativeSummary>&lt;div&gt;A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;On 1 November 2010, the Minister of Justice introduced Bill C-53, An Act to amend the Criminal Code (mega-trials) (Fair and Efficient Criminal Trials Act), in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bill C-53 amends the Criminal Code. Among other things it&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	allows for the appointment of a judge as a case management judge;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	defines the role and the powers of a case management judge;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	allows a joint hearing of preliminary motions involving similar evidence that arise in related but separate trials.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	allows for delayed severance orders;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	streamlines the use of direct indictments preferred under section 577;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	improves the protection of the identity of jurors;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	increases the maximum number of jurors who can hear the evidence on the merits; and&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;•	provides that, in the case of a mistrial, certain decisions made during the trial are binding on the parties in any new trial.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummary>
